</div>

<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">Each of these documents plays a pivotal role: the RC establishes the vehicle’s legitimacy, the PUC ensures environmental compliance, the insurance protects against damage or loss, and the IBA‑approved bilty serves as the official freight contract.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>Failing to provide any one of them can result in delays, fines, or even seizure of your goods at checkpoints.</span></li></ul>

<h3>Why 100 % Declared‑Value Marine Transit Insurance Matters</h3>
<p>While standard cargo insurance may cover a portion of the shipment’s value, a 100 % declared‑value policy guarantees that you receive full compensation if your goods are damaged, lost, or destroyed during transit. This is especially crucial for high‑value items such as electronics, jewelry, or antiques.</p>
<p>The marine transit aspect ensures coverage across all modes of transport—road, rail, or even temporary sea routes used by freight carriers—making it a comprehensive shield against every possible risk.</p>

<p>By assembling the above paperwork and opting for 100 % declared‑value marine transit insurance, you equip yourself with the legal and financial safeguards necessary for a hassle‑free Hyderabad‑to‑Delhi relocation. Prepare these documents early, verify their authenticity, and your move will proceed with confidence and peace of mind.</p></div>
